# VitalPet — Flutter UI Conventions

## Widget structure
Every screen and reusable widget follows this layout:

```dart
// 1. Flutter imports
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter/services.dart'; // for HapticFeedback

// 2. Riverpod
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';

// 3. Third-party (go_router, rive, etc.)
import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';

// 4. Internal feature imports — domain, not presentation
import 'package:vitalpet/features/check_in/domain/check_in_engine.dart';
import 'package:vitalpet/features/pet/domain/pet_state_mapper.dart';

// 5. Internal presentation imports
import 'package:vitalpet/presentation/theme/app_colors.dart';
import 'package:vitalpet/presentation/theme/app_text_styles.dart';

// Screens are ConsumerWidget (reads Riverpod providers)
class CheckInScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  const CheckInScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    // Watch providers first
    final sessionState = ref.watch(checkInSessionProvider);
    final petState = ref.watch(petStateProvider);

    return Scaffold(
      backgroundColor: AppColors.background,
      body: SafeArea(
        child: _CheckInBody(sessionState: sessionState),
      ),
    );
  }
}

// Extract heavy subtrees into private widgets to minimise rebuilds
class _CheckInBody extends StatelessWidget {
  const _CheckInBody({required this.sessionState});
  final CheckInSessionState sessionState;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) { ... }
}
```

## Screen-level rules
- Screens read Riverpod providers via `ref.watch` and dispatch actions via `ref.read(provider.notifier).method()`
- **Zero business logic in screens.** All computation belongs in domain notifiers or pure domain functions
- All navigation uses `context.go()`, `context.push()` from go_router — never `Navigator.push`
- Every screen that loads data must handle `AsyncValue.loading`, `AsyncValue.error`, and `AsyncValue.data`

## WellnessSlider widget
- Full-screen slider, scale 1–10
- Trigger `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` on each integer step (iOS only — wrap in `if (Platform.isIOS)`)
- Set `Semantics(slider: true, value: '$score', min: '1', max: '10')` for accessibility
- This is always the first interaction in a check-in — the score must be captured before any SLM call

## PetRenderer widget (Rive)
```dart
// PetRenderer drives a Rive state machine via typed inputs
// The .riv file (e.g. assets/animations/cat.riv) contains:
//   - StateMachine: "PetStateMachine"
//   - Number input: "vitality" (0–100) — state machine handles all transitions
//   - Boolean inputs: "checkInComplete", "isDead", "isCritical"
//   - Number input: "timeOfDay" (0–3: 0=morning, 1=day, 2=evening, 3=night)

RiveAnimation.asset(
  'assets/animations/${petState.species}.riv',
  stateMachines: const ['PetStateMachine'],
  onInit: (artboard) {
    final controller = StateMachineController.fromArtboard(
      artboard, 'PetStateMachine',
    );
    artboard.addController(controller!);
    _vitalityInput = controller.findInput<double>('vitality');
    _checkInCompleteInput = controller.findInput<bool>('checkInComplete');
  },
)
// Drive from Riverpod:
ref.listen(petVitalityProvider, (_, vitality) {
  _vitalityInput?.value = vitality.toDouble();
});
```
- Always pass `accessibilityLabel: '${petState.name} the ${petState.species}, ${petState.stateName}'`
- Respect `MediaQuery.of(context).disableAnimations` — if true, show a static image fallback

## CompanionBubble widget (Mode 3)
- Renders SLM-generated text as speech bubbles attributed to the pet
- Text must always be the output of `MedicalContentFilter.filter()` — never raw SLM output
- No time pressure UI elements in this widget — remove any countdown or urgency cues
- "I'm done" button always visible, even mid-conversation

## BodyMap widget
- Renders an SVG-based silhouette using `flutter_svg`
- Minimum tap target per region: 44×44 logical pixels (WCAG AA)
- Maximum 3 regions selected simultaneously — selecting a 4th deselects the oldest
- `Semantics(label: 'Body region: ${region.name}, ${selected ? 'selected' : 'not selected'}')` on each tap target

## Theme system
```dart
// ALWAYS use theme tokens — never hardcode
AppColors.background          // background surfaces
AppColors.primary             // teal accent
AppColors.danger              // red — critical state
AppColors.textPrimary         // primary text
AppTextStyles.bodyLarge       // 16sp body
AppTextStyles.headlineMedium  // screen titles
```
- Dark mode is handled in `AppTheme.dark()` — test both modes
- Never hardcode `Color(0xFF...)` values outside `app_colors.dart`
- Never hardcode `TextStyle(fontSize: ...)` outside `app_text_styles.dart`

## Accessibility non-negotiables
- Minimum touch target: 44×44 logical pixels (`ConstrainedBox` or `SizedBox` wrapping `GestureDetector`)
- `Semantics` wrapper on every custom interactive widget
- All Rive animations must have a `Semantics(label: ...)` sibling for screen readers
- Colour is never the sole meaning indicator — pair with text labels
- `MediaQuery.of(context).disableAnimations` must be respected everywhere

## Confetti (milestone streaks)
```dart
// Only for 7, 14, 30, 90-day milestones on check-in completion
ConfettiWidget(
  confettiController: _confettiController,
  blastDirectionality: BlastDirectionality.explosive,
  shouldLoop: false,
  colors: const [AppColors.primary, AppColors.accent, AppColors.warning],
)
// Wrap in: if (!MediaQuery.of(context).disableAnimations)
```
